60*7 is 420. Pages per card: 10. 420 divided by 10 is indeed 42. So, 42 pages. That seems right.\n\nBut just to confirm, maybe I can think of a smaller number. Suppose he had only 5 cards, each page can hold 2 cards. Then total cards divided by pages would be 5/2 which isn't an integer, which makes sense because you can't have half a page. So, the division must be integer here, which it is. So, 42 is the correct number of pages.\n\nI don't see any mistakes in my thinking. The key steps are calculating total cards and then dividing by the capacity per page. So, the answer should be 42.\n\n**Final Answer**\nPuncher needs to buy \\boxed{42} pages.\n</think>\n\nTo determine how many pages Punger needs to buy, let’s break the problem down step by step.\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Calculate the Total Number of Cards\n\nPunger buys 60 packs of baseball cards. Each pack contains 7 cards. Therefore, the total number of cards he has is:\n\n$$\n60 \\text{ packs} \\times 7 \\text{ cards per pack} = 420 \\text{ cards}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Determine the Number of Pages Required\n\nEach page can hold 10 cards. To find out how many pages Punger needs to store all 420 cards, we perform the division:\n\n$$\n\\frac{420 \\text{ cards}}{10 \\text{ cards per page}} = 42 \\text{ pages}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Final Answer:\n\n$$\n\\boxed{42}\n$$<|im_end|>", "source_record": {"question": "Punger collects baseball cards.  He buys 60 packs of baseball cards. Each pack has 7 cards inside. He wants to put these cards in special pages to protect the cards. Each page can hold 10 cards. How many pages does he need to buy?", "answer": "60 packs of cards * 7 cards per pack = <<60*7=420>>420 cards\n420 cards / 10 cards per page = <<420/10=42>>42 pages\n#### 42", "prompt": "Solve the following grade-school math problem. Show your reasoning and put the final answer in \\boxed{}.\n\nProblem: Punger collects baseball cards.  He buys 60 packs of baseball cards. Each pack has 7 cards inside. He wants to put these cards in special pages to protect the cards. Each page can hold 10 cards. How many pages does he need to buy?\nSolution:", "solutions": ["42"], "solution": "42"}, "prompt_tokens": [151644, 872, 198, 50, 3948, 279, 2701, 11972, 34689, 6888, 3491, 13, 6928, 697, 32711, 323, 2182, 279, 1590, 4226, 304, 1124, 79075, 6257, 382, 31198, 25, 30436, 1389, 51207, 19507, 7411, 13, 220, 1260, 49531, 220, 21, 15, 30306, 315, 19507, 7411, 13, 8886, 3769, 702, 220, 22, 7411, 4766, 13, 1260, 6801, 311, 2182, 1493, 7411, 304, 3281, 6816, 311, 6016, 279], "response_tokens": [151667, 198, 32313, 11, 1077, 752, 1430, 311, 7071, 700, 1246, 1657, 6816, 30436, 1389, 3880, 311, 3695, 13, 2055, 11, 566, 49531, 220, 21, 15, 30306, 315, 19507, 7411, 11, 1817, 3769, 702, 220, 22, 7411, 11, 323, 1817, 2150, 646, 3331, 220, 16, 15, 7411, 13, 88190, 11, 1077, 752, 1438, 419, 1495, 3019, 553, 3019, 382, 5338, 11, 358, 1184, 311]}
