at confirms it. Therefore, Jung is 26 years old.\n\nI think that's it. No steps skipped, and all the information is used. I don't see any other possibilities here. So the answer should be 26.\n</think>\n\nWe are given the following information:\n\n- Li is 12 years old.\n- Zhang is twice as old as Li.\n- Jung is 2 years older than Zhang.\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Determine Zhang's age\n\nSince Zhang is twice as old as Li:\n\n$$\n\\text{Zhang's age} = 2 \\times \\text{Li's age} = 2 \\times 12 = 24\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Determine Jung's age\n\nJung is 2 years older than Zhang:\n\n$$\n\\text{Jung's age} = \\text{Zhang's age} + 2 = 24 + 2 = 26\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Final Answer:\n\n$$\n\\boxed{26}\n$$<|im_end|>", "source_record": {"question": "Zhang is twice as old as Li.  Li is 12 years old.  Zhang's brother Jung is 2 years older than Zhang.  How old is Jung?", "answer": "Zhang is 2 * 12 years old = <<2*12=24>>24 years old.\nJung is 2 years + 24 years = <<2+24=26>>26 years old.\n#### 26", "prompt": "Solve the following grade-school math problem. Show your reasoning and put the final answer in \\boxed{}.\n\nProblem: Zhang is twice as old as Li.  Li is 12 years old.  Zhang's brother Jung is 2 years older than Zhang.  How old is Jung?\nSolution:", "solutions": ["26"], "solution": "26"}, "prompt_tokens": [151644, 872, 198, 50, 3948, 279, 2701, 11972, 34689, 6888, 3491, 13, 6928, 697, 32711, 323, 2182, 279, 1590, 4226, 304, 1124, 79075, 6257, 382, 31198, 25, 36020, 374, 10917, 438, 2310, 438, 14511, 13, 220, 14511, 374, 220, 16, 17, 1635, 2310, 13, 220, 36020, 594, 10641, 49332, 374, 220, 17, 1635, 9014, 1091, 36020, 13, 220, 2585, 2310, 374, 49332, 5267, 36842], "response_tokens": [151667, 198, 32313, 11, 1077, 752, 1430, 311, 7071, 700, 1246, 2310, 49332, 374, 13, 2055, 11, 279, 3491, 2727, 429, 36020, 374, 10917, 438, 2310, 438, 14511, 13, 14511, 374, 220, 16, 17, 1635, 2310, 13, 5005, 11, 1052, 594, 36020, 594, 10641, 49332, 11, 879, 374, 220, 17, 1635, 9014, 1091, 36020, 13