late that. 3 multiplied by 17. Let me do 17*3. 10*3 is 30, 7*3 is 21, so total is 51. Then add 2, which makes 53. So the Happy Healthy Family has 53 cows. \n\nWait, so now we have We the People has 17 cows, and the Happy Healthy Family has 53 cows. Therefore, the total number of cows in the ranch would be 17 plus 53. Let me add those up. 17 + 53. 17 + 50 is 67, plus 3 is 70. So the total is 70 cows? That seems straightforward.\n\nLet me double-check my calculations. 3 times 17... 17*3 is indeed 51, plus 2 is 53. So 17 + 53. Yeah, 17 plus 50 is 67, and 67 plus 3 is 70. So the answer should be 70. \n\nHmm, is there any chance I misread the question? Let me check again. The problem says \"two more than three times the number of cows We the People has.\" So that translates correctly. So 3 times 17 is 51, plus 2 is 53. Then total is 17 + 53 = 70. Yep. \n\nAlternatively, maybe write it as 17 + (2 * 3 * 17 / 2)? Wait, no, that's not right. Wait, no, the original problem is \"two more than three times the original amount,\" so 3*C + 2. So if C is 17, then 3*C + 2 = 51 + 2 = 53. Yes. So total is 17 + 53 = 70. \n\nI don't think I made any mistakes here. So the answer is 70 cows in the ranch.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe ranch will have \\boxed{70} cows.\n</think>\n\nTo determine how many cows will be in the ranch altogether, we begin by solving the problem step by step.\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Understand the given information\n\n- We the People has **17 cows**.\n- The Happy Good Healthy Family has **two more than three times the number of cows We the People has**.\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Find the number of cows in the Happy Healthy Family\n\nWe are told that the Happy Healthy Family has **two more than three times** the number of cows We the People has. Mathematically, this can be expressed as:\n\n$$\n\\text{Happy Healthy Family's cows} = 3 \\times \\text{We the People's cows} + 2\n$$\n\nSubstituting the known value of We the People's cows:\n\n$$\n\\text{Happy Healthy Family's cows} = 3 \\times 17 + 2 = 51 + 2 = 53\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 3: Add the number of cows in both families\n\nNow, we add the number of cows from We the People and the Happy Healthy Family:\n\n$$\n\\text{Ranch total cows} = 17 + 53 = 70\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Final Answer:\n\n$$\n\\boxed{70}\n$$<|im_end|>", "source_record": {"question": "We the People has 17 cows. Happy Good Healthy Family has two more than three times the number of cows We the People has. If their cows are taken to a ranch to graze together, how many cows will be in the ranch altogether?", "answer": "Three times the number of cows We the People has is 3*17=<<3*17=51>>51 cows.\nHappy Good Healthy Family has two more than three times the number of cows We the People has, a total of 51+2=53 cows.\nIf the cows are taken to a ranch to graze together, their total will be 53+17=<<53+17=70>>70 cows.\n#### 70", "prompt": "Solve the following grade-school math problem. Show your reasoning and put the final answer in \\boxed{}.\n\nProblem: We the People has 17 cows. Happy Good Healthy Family has two more than three times the number of cows We the People has. If their cows are taken to a ranch to graze together, how many cows will be in the ranch altogether?\nSolution:", "solutions": ["70"], "solution": "70"}, "prompt_tokens": [151644, 872, 198, 50, 3948, 279, 2701, 11972, 34689, 6888, 3491, 13, 6928, 697, 32711, 323, 2182, 279, 1590, 4226, 304, 1124, 79075, 6257, 382, 31198, 25, 1205, 279, 8853, 702, 220, 16, 22, 45166, 13, 23355, 7684, 43354, 12238, 702, 1378, 803, 1091, 2326, 3039, 279, 1372, 315, 45166, 1205, 279, 8853, 702, 13, 1416, 862, 45166, 525, 4429, 311, 264, 38061, 311], "response_tokens": [151667, 198, 32313, 11, 1077, 594, 1490, 13, 2055, 279, 3491, 2727, 429, 1205, 279, 8853, 702, 220, 16, 22, 45166, 13, 5005, 279, 23355, 7684, 43354, 12238, 702, 1378, 803, 1091, 2326, 3039, 279, 1372, 315, 45166, 1205, 279, 8853, 702, 13, 358, 1184, 311, 7071, 700, 1246, 1657, 45166, 525, 304, 279, 38061, 3786, 1283, 807, 