be I can use the formula directly. Let me recall that formula. Yes, A = L × W, so if I plug in the values, it's 7 × 28, which is the same as 7 × (4 × 7) = 4 × 7 × 7 = 4 × 49 = 196. So that confirms it again. \n\nI think that's solid. No issues here. The answer should be 196 square inches, so putting it into a box as requested.\n</think>\n\nTo find the area of the rectangle, we can use the formula for the area of a rectangle:\n\n$$\n\\text{Area} = \\text{length} \\times \\text{width}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Determine the dimensions\n\n- The rectangle is **7 inches wide**.\n- It is **4 times as long** as the width, so its **length** is:\n\n$$\n\\text{length} = 7 \\text{ inches} \\times 4 = 28 \\text{ inches}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Calculate the area\n\n$$\n\\text{Area} = 28 \\text{ inches} \\times 7 \\text{ inches} = 196 \\text{ square inches}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Final Answer:\n\n$$\n\\boxed{196}\n$$<|im_end|>", "source_record": {"question": "You draw a rectangle that is 7 inches wide. It is 4 times as long as it is wide. What is the area of the rectangle?", "answer": "The length of the rectangle is 4 * 7 inches = <<4*7=28>>28 inches.\nThe area of the rectangle is 7 inches * 28 inches = <<7*28=196>>196 square inches.\n#### 196", "prompt": "Solve the following grade-school math problem. Show your reasoning and put the final answer in \\boxed{}.\n\nProblem: You draw a rectangle that is 7 inches wide. It is 4 times as long as it is wide. What is the area of the rectangle?\nSolution:", "solutions": ["196"], "solution": "196"}, "prompt_tokens": [151644, 872, 198, 50, 3948, 279, 2701, 11972, 34689, 6888, 3491, 13, 6928, 697, 32711, 323, 2182, 279, 1590, 4226, 304, 1124, 79075, 6257, 382, 31198, 25, 1446, 4038, 264, 22756, 429, 374, 220, 22, 14924, 6884, 13, 1084, 374, 220, 19, 3039, 438, 1293, 438, 432, 374, 6884, 13, 3555, 374, 279, 3082, 315, 279, 22756, 5267, 36842, 25, 151645, 198, 151644, 77091], "response_tokens": [151667, 198, 32313, 11, 773, 358, 1184, 311, 1477,