 says he wins all of the matches in the first two rounds each of which had 6 matches. So the first two rounds each had 6 matches. Then, in the last round, how many matches? The problem says \"wins half of the 4 matches in the last round.\" So maybe the last round has 4 matches? Let me confirm. The problem says \"the last round\". So if there's a last round, perhaps which is separate. Let me see.\n\nSo maybe the first two rounds each have 6 matches, so total for first two rounds: 6 * 2 = 12. Then, in the last round, there's 4 matches, and he wins half of them, so half of 4 is 2. Then total matches would be 12 (first two) plus 2 (last round) equals 14. \n\nWait, but let me check again. Let me verify the numbers once more. First two rounds: each round 6 matches. So first round: 6 matches, second round: 6 matches. Total 6 + 6 = 12. Last round: 4 matches. Then he wins half of those 4, so 2 matches. Yes. Total wins: 12 + 2 = 14. Therefore, the answer should be 14.\n\nBut wait, hold on. Let me check again. If the problem was translated from another language, maybe the \"last round\" is different. But according to the original problem, it says: \"He wins all of the matches in the first 2 rounds, each of which had 6 matches, then wins half of the 4 matches in the last round.\" So the first two rounds, each had 6 matches. Then the last round has 4 matches, and half of those 4 matches are won. So 4 divided by 2 is 2. So total is 12 + 2 = 14. \n\nAlternatively, maybe the last round is another 4 matches? Let me check once more. The problem says \"the last round.\" If there is only 1 last round, maybe 4 matches? For example, maybe there are two rounds with 4 matches? But no, the problem says \"each of which had 6 matches, then wins half of the 4 matches in the last round.\" So maybe the last round is 4 matches. So 4/2 = 2. \n\nIs there any chance that \"the last round\" might have 2 matches? But that seems unlikely. The problem says \"Half of the 4 matches in the last round\". So 4 matches. Therefore, 2 wins. So total matches: 14. \n\nBut just to make sure, let me think of another way. So total matches: first two rounds: 6*2=12. Last round: 4 matches. So total 16 matches. Half of 4 is 2. 12+2=14. So 14 matches. Therefore, the answer is \\boxed{14}.\n\nI think that's correct. No mistakes in my reasoning. Each step adds up, and the numbers are straight forward. First two rounds: 6x2=12. Last round: half of 4 is 2. So total 14. Yeah, that seems right. I don't see any errors in my thinking here. \n\n**Final Answer**\n\\boxed{14}\n</think>\n\nTo determine how many matches Brendan won throughout the competition, we'll break down the problem into logical steps.\n\n---\n\n### **Step 1: Matches in the First Two Rounds**\n\n- Each of the first two rounds involved 6 matches.\n- There are **two rounds**, so total matches in the first two rounds:\n  $$\n  6 \\, \\text{matches} \\times 2 = 12 \\, \\text{matches}\n  $$\n\n---\n\n### **Step 2: Matches in the Last Round**\n\n- The problem states that Brendan \"wins half of the 4 matches in the last round.\"\n- Therefore, half of 4 matches is:\n  $$\n  \\frac{4}{2} = 2 \\, \\text{matches}\n  $$\n\n---\n\n### **Step 3: Total Matches Won**\n\n- Total matches won: \n  $$\n  12 \\, (\\text{first two rounds}) + 2 \\, (\\text{last round}) = 14\n  $$\n\n---\n\n### **Final Answer**\n\n$$\n\\boxed{14}\n$$<|im_end|>", "source_record": {"question": "Brendan has entered a kickboxing competition and wins matches against multiple contestants. He wins all of the matches in the first 2 rounds, each of which had 6 matches, then wins half of the 4 matches in the last round. How many matches did Brendan win throughout the competition?", "answer": "In the first 2 rounds, Brendan wins a total of 2 rounds * 6 matches per round = <<2*6=12>>12 matches.\nIn the last round, Brendan wins half of the matches which is 4 matches / 2 = <<4/2=2>>2 matches.\nThroughout the competition, Brendan has therefore won 12 + 2 = <<12+2=14>>14 matches.\n#### 14", "prompt": "Solve the following grade-school math problem. Show your reasoning and put the final answer in \\boxed{}.\n\nProblem: Brendan has entered a kickboxing competition and wins matches against multiple contestants. He wins all of the matches in the first 2 rounds, each of which had 6 matches, then wins half of the 4 matches in the last round. How many matches did Brendan win throughout the competition?\nSolution:", "solutions": ["14"], "solution": "14"}, "prompt_tokens": [151644, 872, 198, 50, 3948, 279, 2701, 11972, 34689, 6888, 3491, 13, 6928, 697, 32711, 323, 2182, 279, 1590, 4226, 304, 1124, 79075, 6257, 382, 31198, 25, 55843, 702, 10636, 264, 10323, 89174, 10707, 323, 14816, 9071, 2348, 5248, 74424, 13, 1260, 14816, 678, 315, 279, 9071, 304, 279, 1156, 220, 17, 19531, 11, 1817, 315, 892, 1030, 220, 21, 9071, 11, 1221, 14816], "response_tokens": [151667, 198, 32313, 11, 773, 55843, 594, 3491, 374, 911, 37614, 1246, 1657, 9071, 566, 2765, 304, 264, 10323, 89174, 10707, 13, 6771, 752, 1430, 311, 7071, 419, 700, 3019, 553, 3019, 13, 4710, 5338, 11, 1077, 752, 312, 2454, 279, 3491, 304, 847, 1828, 4244, 311, 1281, 2704, 358, 3535, 432, 13, 55843, 2765, 678, 279, 9071, 304, 279, 1156, 1378, 19531, 13]}
