, and then add 5 inches to Kelly. Which gives the same result. So 72 - 3 is 69, plus 5 is 74. Yeah, that seems right.\n\nBut let me think if there's another way to approach it. Maybe using equations. Let me assign variables. Let Jess's height be J. Then, according to the problem, Jess is 72 inches tall, so J = 72 inches. \n\nNow, the problem states that Kelly is 3 inches shorter than Jess. So Kelly = Jess - 3. Therefore, Kelly = 72 - 3 = 69 inches. \n\nThen, Jana is 5 inches taller than Kelly, so Jana = Kelly + 5 = 69 + 5 = 74 inches. \n\nAlternatively, if I think of the relationships backwards. From Jana, since Jana is 5 inches taller than Kelly, Jana = Kelly + 5. And Kelly is 3 inches shorter than Jess, so Kelly = Jess - 3. Therefore, Jana = Jess - 3 + 5 = Jess + 2. \n\nSo, Jana's height is Jess's height plus 2 inches. Therefore, since Jess is 72 inches, Jana is 72 + 2 = 74 inches tall. \n\nAll methods seem to lead to the same answer. So I think 74 inches is correct.\n\nWait, just to be thorough, let me check again. Let me multiply all in steps:\n\n- Jess: 72\n\n- Kelly is 3 shorter: 72 - 3 = 69\n\n- Jana is 5 taller: 69 + 5 = 74\n\nYep, that works. So no mistakes here. The answer should be 74. I don't see any errors in my reasoning. Therefore, Jana is 74 inches tall.\n</think>\n\nTo determine how tall Jana is, we are given the following relationships between the heights of Jess, Kelly, and Jana:\n\n- **Jess is 72 inches tall.**\n- **Kelly is 3 inches shorter than Jess.**\n- **Jana is 5 inches taller than Kelly.**\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Calculate Kelly's height\n\nSince **Jess is 3 inches shorter than Kelly**, we find:\n\n$$\n\\text{Kelly's height} = 72 - 3 = 69 \\text{ inches}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Calculate Jana's height\n\nNow, **Jana is 5 inches taller than Kelly**, so:\n\n$$\n\\text{Jana's height} = 69 + 5 = 74 \\text{ inches}\n$$\n\n---\n\n### Final Answer\n\n$$\n\\boxed{74}\n$$<|im_end|>", "source_record": {"question": "Jana is 5 inches taller than Kelly, and Kelly is 3 inches shorter than Jess. If Jess is 72 inches tall, how tall is Jana?", "answer": "Kelly is 72-3=<<72-3=69>>69 inches tall.\nJana is 69+5=<<69+5=74>>74 inches tall.\n#### 74", "prompt": "Solve the following grade-school math problem. Show your reasoning and put the final answer in \\boxed{}.\n\nProblem: Jana is 5 inches taller than Kelly, and Kelly is 3 inches shorter than Jess. If Jess is 72 inches tall, how tall is Jana?\nSolution:", "solutions": ["74"], "solution": "74"}, "prompt_tokens": [151644, 872, 198, 50, 3948, 279, 2701, 11972, 34689, 6888, 3491, 13, 6928, 697, 32711, 323, 2182, 279, 1590, 4226, 304, 1124, 79075, 6257, 382, 31198, 25, 619, 3362, 374, 220, 20, 14924, 49909, 1091, 18661, 11, 323, 18661, 374, 220, 18, 14924, 23327, 1091, 23039, 13, 1416, 23039, 374, 220, 22, 17, 14924, 16217, 11, 1246, 16217, 374, 619, 3362, 5267, 36842, 25], "response_tokens": [151667, 198, 32313, 11, 1077, 594, 1490, 13, 2055, 279, 3491, 2727, 619, 3362, 374, 220, 20, 14924, 49909, 1091, 18661, 11, 323, 18661, 374, 220, 18, 14924, 23327, 1091, 23039, 13, 23039, 374, 220, 22, 17, 14924, 16217, 13, 358, 1184, 311, 1477, 700, 1246, 16217, 619, 3362, 374, 13, 88190, 11, 1077, 752, 1438, 419, 1495, 3019, 553, 3019, 382, 5338, 11]}
